               <ul><li>WRIRP – Writing scale<br></li></ul></li></ul><h3>Jurisdiction</h3><ul><li>NT – National<br></li><li>NP – National public<br></li><li>NR – National private<br></li><li>NL – Large city<br></li><li>AL – Alabama<br></li><li>AK – Alaska<br></li><li>AZ – Arizona<br></li><li>AR – Arkansas<br></li><li>CA – California<br></li><li>CO – Colorado<br></li><li>CT – Connecticut<br></li><li>DE – Delaware<br></li><li>DC – District of Columbia<br></li><li>DS – DoDEA<br></li><li>FL – Florida<br></li><li>GA – Georgia<br></li><li>HI – Hawaii<br></li><li>ID – Idaho<br></li><li>IL – Illinois<br></li><li>IN – Indiana<br></li><li>IA – Iowa<br></li><li>KS – Kansas<br></li><li>KY – Kentucky<br></li><li>LA – Louisiana<br></li><li>ME – Maine<br></li><li>MD – Maryland<br></li><li>MA – Massachusetts<br></li><li>MI – Michigan<br></li><li>MN – Minnesota<br></li><li>MS – Mississippi<br></li><li>MO – Missouri<br></li><li>MT – Montana<br></li><li>NE – Nebraska<br></li><li>NV – Nevada<br></li><li>NH – New Hampshire<br></li><li>NJ – New Jersey<br></li><li>NM – New Mexico<br></li><li>NY – New York<br></li><li>NC – North Carolina<br></li><li>ND – North Dakota<br></li><li>OH – Ohio<br></li><li>OK – Oklahoma<br></li><li>OR – Oregon<br></li><li>PA – Pennsylvania<br></li><li>RI – Rhode Island<br></li><li>SC – South Carolina<br></li><li>SD – South Dakota<br></li><li>TN – Tennessee<br></li><li>TX – Texas<br></li><li>UT – Utah<br></li><li>VT – Vermont<br></li><li>VA – Virginia<br></li><li>WA – Washington<br></li><li>WV – West Virginia<br></li><li>WI – Wisconsin<br></li><li>WY – Wyoming<br></li><li>DD – DoDEA/DDESS<br></li><li>DO – DoDEA/DoDDS<br></li><li>XQ – Albuquerque<br></li><li>XA – Atlanta<br></li><li>XU – Austin<br></li><li>XM – Baltimore City<br></li><li>XB – Boston<br></li><li>XT – Charlotte<br></li><li>XC – Chicago<br></li><li>XX – Clark County (NV)<br></li><li>XV – Cleveland<br></li><li>XS – Dallas<br></li><li>XY – Denver<br></li><li>XR – Detroit<br></li><li>XW – District of Columbia (DCPS)<br></li><li>XE – Duval County (FL)<br></li><li>XZ – Fort Worth (TX)<br></li><li>XF – Fresno<br></li><li>XG – Guilford County (NC)<br></li><li>XO – Hillsborough County (FL)<br></li><li>XH – Houston<br></li><li>XJ – Jefferson County (KY)<br></li><li>XL – Los Angeles​<br></li><li>XI – Miami-Dade<br></li><li>XK – Milwaukee<br></li><li>XN – New York City<br></li><li>XP – Philadelphia<br></li><li>XD – San Diego<br></li><li>YA – Shelby County (TN)<br></li><li>YB - Orange County (FL)</li><li>​XFCA – California without Fresno<br></li><li>XLCA – California without Los Angeles</li><li>XDCA – California without San Diego</li><li>​QQCA – California without any TUDAs</li><li>XYCO – Colorado without Denver</li><li>XWDC – District of Columbia without DCPS</li><li>XEFL – Florida without Duval County</li><li>XOFL – Florida without Hillsborough County</li><li>XIFL – Florida without Miami-Dade</li><li>YBFL – Florida without Orange County</li><li>QQFL – Florida without any TUDAs</li><li>XAGA – Georgia without Atlanta</li><li>XCIL – Illinois without Chicago</li><li>XJKY – Kentucky without Jefferson County</li><li>XMMD – Maryland without Baltimore</li><li>XBMA – Massachusetts without Boston</li><li>XRMI – Michigan without Detroit</li><li>XXNV – Nevada without Clark County</li><li>XQNM – New Mexico without Albuquerque</li><li>XNNY – New York without New York City</li><li>XTNC – North Carolina without Charlotte</li><li>XGNC – North Carolina without Guilford County</li><li>QQNC – North Carolina without any TUDAs</li><li>XVOH – Ohio without Cleveland</li><li>XPPA – Pennsylvania without Philadelphia</li><li>YATN – Tennessee without Shelby County</li><li>XUTX – Texas without Austin</li><li>XSTX – Texas without Dallas</li><li>XZTX – Texas without Forth Worth</li><li>XHTX – Texas without Houston</li><li>QQTX – Texas without any TUDAs</li><li>XKWI – Wisconsin without Milwaukee</li><li>AS – American Samoa<br></li><li>GU – Guam<br></li><li>PR – Puerto Rico<br></li><li>VI – Virgin Islands<br></li></ul> 
         <a id="cohort"></a> 
         <h3>Grade/Cohort<br></h3><ul><li>Use either grade or cohort, newer calls only take cohort<br></li><li>Grade 
               <ul><li>4</li><li>8</li><li>12</li></ul></li><li>Cohort<br> 
               <ul><li>1 = Grade 4 or Age 9<br></li><li>2 = Grade 8 or Age 13<br></li><li>3 = Grade 12 or Age 17<br></li></ul></li></ul>​ 
         <a id="year"></a> 
         <h3>Year</h3><ul><li><Year>R2&#160; e.g., 1990R2 (R2 stands for accommodations not permitted sample)<br></li><li><Year>R3&#160; e.g., 2016R3 (R3 stands for accommodations permitted sample)<br></li><li>If R2 or R3 is not indicated, default is R3<br></li><li>Base, Current, and Prior are keywords 
               <ul><li>Base – first assessment year<br></li><li>Current – most recent assessment year<br></li><li>Prior – second most recent assessment year<br></li></ul></li></ul><h3>StatType</h3><ul><li>MN:MN – Mean<br></li><li>RP:RP – Row percent<br></li><li>ALD:BA – Discrete achievement level – At Basic<br></li><li>ALD:PR – Discrete achievement level – At Proficient<br></li><li>ALD:AD – Discrete achievement level – At Advanced<br></li><li>ALC:BB – Cumulative achievement level&#160; - Below Basic<br></li><li>ALC:AB – Cumulative achievement level – At or above Basic<br></li><li>ALC:AP – Cumulative achievement level – At or above Proficient<br></li><li>ALC:AD – Cumulative achievement level – At Advanced<br></li><li>SD:SD – Standard deviations<br></li><li>PC:P1 – 10th percentile<br></li><li>PC:P2 – 25th percentile<br></li><li>PC:P5 – 50th percentile<br></li><li>PC:P7 – 75th percentile<br></li><li>PC:P9 – 90th percentile</li><li>DP:DP&#160;–&#160;Distribution percentages in 10-point scale score intervals&#160;&#160;<br></li></ul><h3>Categoryindex<br></h3><ul><li>Categories are also known as variable values.<br></li><li>For example, for SDRACE, White = 1, Black = 2, Hispanic = 3<br></li><li>For example, for GENDER+SDRACE, 1+3 returns male Hispanic, 2+2 returns female Black, encode as 1%2B3,2%2B2</li><li>CategoryIndex&#160;is not required in requests, If omitted all the values are returned<br></li><li>NAEP Variable Values List API<br>
               <ul><li>Returns variables values for the set of variables requested.<br>
                     <ul><li>Returns list&#160;of Varnames and its values.<br></li><li>Use Value as categoryindex&#160;parameters for&#160;the main NAEP Data Service API.<br></li></ul></li><li>Parameters<br> 
                     <ul><li>type = VariableValues<br></li><li>NAEPIDs = Variable ID's<br></li></ul></li><li>Example Call<br><a href="/Dataservice/GetAdhocData.aspx?type=VariableValues&amp;NAEPIDs=Gender%2cSDRACE">https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/Dataservice/GetAdhocData.aspx?type=VariableValues&amp;NAEPIDs=Gender,SDRACE</a><br></li></ul></li></ul>​​ 
         <h3>Variable<br></h3><ul><li>Student demographic groups&#160;or survey question variable or index.<br></li><li>Commonly used variables 
               <ul><li>TOTAL – All students<br></li><li>SDRACE – Race/ethnicity used to report trends<br></li><li>SRACE10&#160;– Race/ethnicity using 2011 guidelines<br></li><li>GENDER – Gender<br></li><li>SLUNCH3&#160;– National School Lunch Program eligibility<br></li><li>PARED&#160;– Parental education level<br></li><li>SCHTYPE&#160;– Public or nonpublic school<br></li><li>CHRTRPT&#160;– School identified as charter<br></li><li>UTOL4&#160;– School location<br></li><li>CENSREG&#160;– Region of the country<br></li><li>IEP&#160;– Disability status of student, including those with 504 plan<br></li><li>LEP&#160;– Status as English language learner<br></li></ul></li><li>NAEP Variable List API 
               <ul><li>Returns a set of independent variables for each year and&#160;sample for&#160;the specified&#160;subject and cohort<br> 
